<title>USA: Chrysler to idle Belvidere, Ill., plant - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Chrysler to idle Belvidere, Ill., plant - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sluggish sales of small Dodge and Plymouth Neons are prompting Chrysler Corp to idle its Belvidere, Ill., plant next week, The Wall Street Journal reported Friday.</p>
<p>Chrysler is not alone when it comes to slow-selling small cars, the story says.</p>
<p>&quot;It's also a Ford problem and a General Motors problem,&quot; Bear Sterns analyst Nick Lobaccaro says in the story.</p>
</text>
